# ripgrep / fd ignore — GENERATED output only (EI-25828526343827983).
#
# Read by ripgrep and fd, not by git. public/internal/docs is ~3,400 TRACKED,
# generated HTML pages (~385 MB). Nearly any identifier an agent searches for
# appears in them, on lines up to ~700,000 characters long, so one search from
# `apps` or the repo root returned ~300 MB (measured 2026-10-13). The source is
# the docs corpus, which docs:search / search:fulltext already cover.
#
# Why here and not in the repo-root .ignore: ripgrep applies an anchored pattern
# from an ignore file ABOVE the search root only to that root's immediate
# children, so a root-level entry is skipped when the search starts in `apps`.
# This file is read whenever a walk enters apps/operator, so it holds from the
# repo root, `apps`, and `apps/operator`. (Searching from apps/operator/public
# itself is the one root it does not cover.) A file named explicitly is still
# searched. Pinned by
# packages/operator-core/lib/code-intelligence/ripgrep-generated-trees-ignore.test.ts.
/public/internal/docs/
